.TH ARES_CANCEL_BY_ARG 3 "18 October 2026"
.SH NAME
ares_cancel_by_arg \- Cancel requests matching a callback argument
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ares.h>

void ares_cancel_by_arg(ares_channel_t *\fIchannel\fP, void *\fIarg\fP)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBares_cancel_by_arg(3)\fP function cancels all pending lookups/requests
on the name service channel identified by \fIchannel\fP whose callback
argument matches \fIarg\fP. Matching callbacks are invoked with a status of
.BR ARES_ECANCELLED .
If multiple pending requests use the same callback argument (including
.BR NULL ),
all such requests will be cancelled.

If a cancelled request callback adds a new request to the channel, that request
will \fInot\fP be cancelled by the current invocation of
\fBares_cancel_by_arg(3)\fP.
.SH AVAILABILITY
This function was first introduced in c-ares version 1.35.0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ares_cancel (3),
.BR ares_destroy (3),
.BR ares_init (3)
